# keel-mariadb: the socket units of mariadb-server stay off (keel-mariadb#29).
#
# mariadb.socket has ListenStream=3306, which systemd binds as [::]:3306, on
# every address of the machine, uplink included. With the socket active the
# server gets its listeners from systemd, and bind-address, which keel and
# this layer use to keep 3306 on loopback and on the mesh, has no effect.
# mariadb-extra.socket also starts mariadb.service and gives it sockets, so
# it stays off too: the server then opens all its listeners from its own
# configuration.
#
# Debian's package enables neither, but the first boot of systemd enables
# every unit that no preset disables, and pct create of Proxmox VE makes the
# first start of a container a first boot. The package also masks both
# (postinst), because a preset is read at a first boot only.
disable mariadb.socket
disable mariadb-extra.socket
